6. A pitch script you can adapt
If I were using these presentations as a reference for a new ETHGlobal submission, I'd draft the spoken pitch in this format:

Writing
[Opening: 0:00–0:20]
Imagine you're [specific user] trying to [specific task]. Today, you have to [describe the existing difficulty]. We built [project name] to solve this.

[Solution: 0:20–0:40]

[Project name] is a [simple description of the product]. It lets users [main benefit] by [distinctive mechanism].

[Demo: 0:40–1:50]

Let me show you how it works.

First, [show the initial user action]. As you can see, [show the system response].

Next, [show the central technical action]. This is where [key integration or mechanism] comes in.

And here's the result: [show a real, verifiable outcome].

[Technical differentiation: 1:50–2:40]

The important part is how we achieved this. Instead of [existing approach or limitation], we use [technical contribution]. This enables [specific benefit] while [relevant trade-off, security property or efficiency gain].

[Proof and conclusion: 2:40–3:00]

We built [specific completed functionality] during the hackathon, and the demonstration shows [what is verified]. The next step is [one realistic next milestone].

That's [project name]: [one-sentence summary]. Thank you.
